//! The `interpolate-size` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property allows
//! you to enable [animations](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Animations)
//! and [transitions](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Transitions) between a
//! `<length-percentage>` value and an `intrinsic size`, `fit-content`, or `max-content`.
//!
//! Initial: numeric-only. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - allow-keywords: Enables
//! [interpolation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Interpolation) between a
//! `length-percentage` value and an intrinsic size value, to allow animation between the two.
//! - numeric-only: The default behavior — intrinsic size values cannot be interpolated.
//!
//! Grammar: numeric-only | allow-keywords
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-5/#propdef-interpolate-size
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/interpolate-size
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

